{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 11,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.046,
            0.347,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.087,
            0.73,
            0.107
          ],
          "content": "The ratio of weight to price of the Himachal tea is 200 : 200."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.107,
            0.848,
            0.181
          ],
          "content": "What is the weight to price ratio of the Meghalaya tea? Is it 1 : 800? This would not be appropriate, because we considered the weight in grams in the case of Himachal. So, the weight to price ratio is 1000 : 800 in Meghalaya after we convert the weight to grams."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.18,
            0.847,
            0.217
          ],
          "content": "To check if the ratios are proportional, we need to see if both ratios are the same in their simplest forms."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.216,
            0.641,
            0.236
          ],
          "content": "The Himachal tea ratio in its simplest form is 1 : 1."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.235,
            0.652,
            0.255
          ],
          "content": "The Meghalaya tea ratio in its simplest form is 5 : 4."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.254,
            0.492,
            0.273
          ],
          "content": "So, the ratios are not proportional."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.275,
            0.508,
            0.298
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Which tea is more expensive? Why?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.307,
            0.842,
            0.357
          ],
          "content": "**Note to the Teacher:** Encourage a discussion on the more expensive tea, how they came to their conclusions and what the reasons for that tea being more expensive could be."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.373,
            0.848,
            0.429
          ],
          "content": "To answer the question as to which tea is more expensive, we should compare the price of tea for the same weight in both places. What is the price of 1 kg of tea from Meghalaya? It is ₹800."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.429,
            0.848,
            0.466
          ],
          "content": "In Himachal, if 200 g of tea costs rupees 200, what is the cost of 1 kg of tea?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.466,
            0.799,
            0.508
          ],
          "content": "Let us say that the price of 1 kg of tea is x rupees. 200 g is 15 of 1 kg. So, $\\frac{1}{5} \\times \\overline{x} = 200.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.507,
            0.497,
            0.529
          ],
          "content": "Multiplying both sides by 5, we get"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.41,
            0.535,
            0.587,
            0.562
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{1}{5} \\times x \\times 5 = 200 \\times 5",
          "image_source": "images/page_11_equation_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.417,
            0.565,
            0.579,
            0.595
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{1}{5} \\times x \\times 5 = 1000",
          "image_source": "images/page_11_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.452,
            0.595,
            0.545,
            0.615
          ],
          "content": "x = 1000.",
          "image_source": "images/page_11_equation_15.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.619,
            0.847,
            0.656
          ],
          "content": "So, the cost of 1 kg of tea is ₹800 in Meghalaya and ₹1,000 in Himachal Pradesh."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.656,
            0.75,
            0.677
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, the tea from Himachal Pradesh is more expensive."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.686,
            0.849,
            0.781
          ],
          "content": "**Activity 1:** Take your favourite dish. Find out all the ingredients and their respective quantities needed to make the dish for your family. Suppose you are celebrating a festival and you want to invite 15 guests. Find out the quantities of the ingredients required to cook the same dish for them."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.795,
            0.293,
            0.82
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.831,
            0.848,
            0.871
          ],
          "content": "1. The Earth travels approximately 940 million kilometres around the Sun in a year. How many kilometres will it travel in a week?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.879,
            0.849,
            0.919
          ],
          "content": "2. A mason is building a house in the shape shown in the diagram. He needs to construct both the outer walls and the inner wall that"
